 "level_notes": {"0": "Defined by rustc's data structures (rustc_middle::mir::syntax); Miri is an interpreter for MIR that detects undefined behaviour, and MiniRust is a reference-interpreter-style specification of a MIR-like core language.", "1": "No stable specification: RFC 1211 introduced MIR, RFC 2094 (NLL) defines borrow checking on it; the generated rustc API docs are the reference for its constructs. std::intrinsics::mir allows writing MIR directly (unstable, for tests).", "2": "The rustc dev guide chapters are the main explanation."},
